# artefactos de compilacion
build/

# CLion's CMakeLists.txt is IDE-only tooling for the desktop emulator (see
# its own header comment); these are its out-of-source build directories.
cmake-build-*/

# cacheas y artefactos regenerables del taller
tools/downloads/
tools/__pycache__/
__pycache__/
tools/sheet.png
tools/import_sheet.png
tools/emitted_sprites.js
tools/demo_anim.js
tools/demo_compare.js

.DS_Store
tools/pmd_cache/
tools/pokeapi_cache/
tools/pokeapi_cache.old/

# Claude Code's own local tooling state (permission allowlists, a runtime
# session lock with a live PID) -- not part of the game, not portable to
# another machine.
.claude/

# The sprite bundles ARE committed, and that is deliberate. They have to be
# served same-origin from GitHub Pages: release assets send no CORS headers at
# all, so a browser can never fetch() one, however convenient it would be to
# keep them out of the repo. Tested with an Origin header; there is no header
# to be had. Pages sends access-control-allow-origin: *.

# The loose per-species sprite packs are build INTERMEDIATES, not artefacts.
# They are what pack_bundle.py reads to build web/sprites-*.pak, and the .pak
# files are what actually gets distributed -- so tracking both puts the same
# ~105 MB of sprite data in the repo twice. Regenerate with:
#
#   python3 tools/pack_pmd.py            # or: kanto / johto / hoenn
#   python3 tools/make_thumbs.py
#
# CREDITS.md already recommends exactly this: ship the code and the scripts and
# let each user package the sprites from the original sources.
tools/sdcard/mons/*.bin

# Emulator save files and downloaded generator intermediates: local scratch, not
# artefacts. They were committed by accident once.
tamapoke.nvs
tamapoke.nvs.*
tools/_*.svg
backups/

# CREDITS.md flags both of these as NOT safe to publish as committed headers:
#   avatars.h -- real Nintendo/Game Freak sprites from the pret/pokered
#     disassembly, not licensed for redistribution. The documented approach
#     is to ship tools/gen_avatars.py instead, so each user fetches the art
#     themselves (needs only curl).
#   backs.h / tools/backs/*.png -- provenance never established. CREDITS.md
#     says explicitly: confirm the licence or replace them before this repo
#     is public. Until then, excluded rather than guessed at.
# Both still exist locally for anyone who already has them; this only keeps
# them out of a public push.
avatars.h
backs.h
tools/backs/*.png
